{"text": "MEETING NOTES -- PRIVILEGED & CONFIDENTIAL / ATTORNEY WORK PRODUCT\nIbarra Kettleman LLP                      Matter No. 2026-0417-CORP\nDate: 9/22/2026 (Tues.), 10:00-11:35 a.m., our Bozeman office\nPresent: Hunter Abernathy-Sloane (client); Georgia Sloane (spouse, by phone,\nfirst 20 min only); Soledad Ibarra (SI); Billy Tran, paralegal (notes)\n\n1. Background\nHunter owns 70% of Three Forks Millwork & Cabinet Co. (\"Three Forks\" or \"TFM\"), a\nMontana S corp, EIN 81-4472093. The other 30% sits in the Estate of Wade R. Abernathy --\nHunter's older brother, who died 02/11/2025. Wade's widow, Marisol Abernathy, is\npersonal rep (Gallatin County probate, Cause No. DP-25-0193). Hunter says\nMarisol \"will sign anything if the check clears.\" SI wants her separately represented\nand told him so twice.\n\nReason for selling, per Hunter (NOT to be shared with buyer): he had a stent placed in June\nand his cardiologist wants him off the shop floor. Georgia confirmed; she keeps the\nbooks and is ready to be done.\n\n2. The offer\nBuyer is Ridgeline Building Products Holdings, Inc. (\"Ridgeline\"), Boise. LOI dated\nAugust 28, 2026. Headline price $6.4 million:\n   - $5,150,000 cash at close\n   - $750k seller note, 6%, five years, subordinated to Ridgeline's senior lender\n   - earn-out up to $500,000 on 2027 EBITDA\n   - working capital peg $1.1MM; 10% escrow ($640,000) for 18 months\nStructure: stock sale with a Section 338(h)(10) election. Buyer wants a Form 8594-style\nallocation schedule anyway (IRC § 1060 by analogy). Target close Nov. 30, 2026.\nCode name on all buyer paper is \"Project Larch\".\n\nBuyer's counsel: Preston Achebe, Esq., Lowell & Achebe PLLC, pachebe@lowellachebe.example,\n208.555.0164. Mr. Achebe has already asked for three years of returns.\n\n3. Real estate\nShop and yard at 4410 Frontage Road, Belgrade, MT 59714 are NOT in the company. Title\nis in H&G Sloane Properties, L.L.C. (Hunter and Georgia, 50/50). Ridgeline wants a 10-year\nlease at $14,500/mo with an option to buy. Hunter would rather sell the dirt outright.\n\n4. Debt / guaranty\nFirst Gallatin Bank & Trust line of credit, Loan No. 7700-218845, balance about\n$412,000. Hunter signed a personal guaranty; Wade did too, so the estate is on the hook.\nFirst Gallatin needs for the release: Hunter DOB 7/4/1963, SSN xxx-xx-5222, MT driver's\nlicense 0704196341207. Payoff wire goes to ABA 119762284, acct 0048-771-9023.\n\n5. People issues\nDmitri Vasquez-Koval is the only CNC programmer they have. Ridgeline will want a\nretention agreement. Hunter mentioned, quietly, that Dmitri is on a TPS work permit\nthat runs out 3/2027. SI: do not volunteer, do not conceal; goes in the disclosure\nschedule if asked. Hunter wants Dmitri to get $38,000 out of proceeds as a thank-you.\n\n6. Data room\nRidgeline opened one at https://dataroom.ridgelinebp.example/project-larch. Hunter's login is\nhsloane_tfm, temp password Larch!2026#mw (told him to change it today).\n\nTo do\n- SI: engagement letter + conflict waiver re estate; call Mr. Achebe re exclusivity (45 days?)\n- Billy: order UCC and lien searches; calendar LOI expiry\n- Hunter: send 2023-2025 returns and the equipment list. Cell (406) 555-0119,\n  hunter@threeforksmillwork.example", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "494 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Hunter Abernathy-Sloane", "Georgia Sloane", "Soledad Ibarra", "Billy Tran", "Marisol Abernathy", "Preston Achebe", "Hunter", "Dmitri Vasquez-Koval"], "companies": ["Ibarra Kettleman LLP", "Three Forks Millwork & Cabinet Co.", "Gallatin County probate", "Ridgeline Building Products Holdings, Inc.", "H&G Sloane Properties, L.L.C.", "Lowell & Achebe PLLC", "First Gallatin Bank & Trust", "Allegheny Bank & Trust", "Ridgeline", "Three Forks Millwork"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.30000000074505806, "modelMs": 38029.90000000037, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein",